{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvaghSpciWrjwGW2jBsp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The remaining N0 loops are mostly \"stuck\" reconsideration loops. The model meets an apparent contradiction or ambiguity, then cycles verbatim through lines like \"Is it possible that…\", \"But if…\", \"However, I should also consider…\", \"Let's try a different interpretation\", often as markdown bullets. So the hesitation state seems to persist and is now voiced through other words. This fits the earlier finding that n998's own activation did not drop: we cut the conversion of hesitation into \"Wait\", not the hesitation itself. \"Wait\" was the dominant self-reinforcing token, so the question is whether any substitute word now shows the same growth with position, which would be the signature of a spiral and a candidate second mechanism. I will count rates per 1k tokens of each hesitation word by position bin in cut answers, for N0 against the original. A word whose rate rises steeply with position in N0 (as Wait did originally) would be the next target. Flat rates would mean the remaining loops are copy lock-in rather than a word-specific spiral.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: after n998 removal, another hesitation word (But/Is it possible/However/...) carries a self-reinforcing spiral in N0 cut answers\nFAM = {'Wait': r'\\bWait\\b', 'But': r'\\bBut\\b', 'However': r'\\bHowever\\b', 'Is it poss': r'\\bIs it possible\\b', 'Maybe': r'\\bMaybe\\b',\n       'Actually': r'\\bActually\\b', 'Hmm': r'\\bHmm\\b', 'Altern': r'\\bAlternatively\\b', \"Let's try\": r\"\\bLet'?s try\\b\", 'check': r'(?i)\\b(re-?check|double[- ]check)',\n       'So': r'(?m)^\\W*So\\b', 'If': r'(?m)^\\W*If\\b', 'Yes': r'\\bYes\\b', 'No,': r'\\bNo,'}\nBINS = [0, 1000, 2000, 4000, 8000, 16000, 32769]\ndef fam_rates(name, cut_flag):\n    cnt = {f: np.zeros(len(BINS)-1) for f in FAM}; tot = np.zeros(len(BINS)-1)\n    for r in G[name]:\n        for s in r['samples']:\n            if s['cut'] != cut_flag: continue\n            t = s['text']; cpt = len(t) / max(s['tokens'], 1)\n            ntok = s['tokens']\n            for b in range(len(BINS)-1):\n                tot[b] += max(0, min(ntok, BINS[b+1]) - BINS[b])\n            for f, pat in FAM.items():\n                for m in re.finditer(pat, t):\n                    p = m.start() / cpt\n                    b = np.searchsorted(BINS, p, side='right') - 1\n                    if 0 <= b < len(BINS)-1: cnt[f][b] += 1\n    return {f: cnt[f] / np.maximum(tot, 1) * 1000 for f in FAM}\nfor name in ['orig', 'N0']:\n    for cf in [True, False]:\n        R = fam_rates(name, cf)\n        print(f\"== {name} {'CUT' if cf else 'FIN'} (bins 0-1k,1-2k,2-4k,4-8k,8-16k,16-32k)\")\n        print('   ' + ' | '.join(f\"{f}:\" + ','.join(f\"{v:.1f}\" for v in R[f]) for f in FAM))\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_read_input_tokens":18465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fc44c029-332b-4924-9870-b11affa1f97a","uuid":"ee46df5d-2ff0-4f92-8cb3-ccba69725f2e","timestamp":"2026-11-11T05:23:59.303Z","request_id":"req_011CgvaghKd7UMNrVfu7CoxV"}
